            "review_title": "Review at Shinbashi Japanese Restaurant",
            "review_text": "DrMiriam\nAlbuquerque, New Mexico40 contributions\n0\nRats\nOct 2018 • Friends\nWe had a very nice sushi dinner at this restaurant last night. Unfortunately, when we were sitting around talking after most of the diners had left the room, we started to hear noises coming from the ceiling. The ceiling consists of a false ceiling made to look like rice paper, with back-lighting. This vividly illuminated large numbers of rats that started to run across the ceiling panels. We decided to leave and, just as we were getting up, one of the ceiling panels gave way like a trap-door as rats ran over it—but fortunately they scrabbled to safety, rather than falling through onto the dining room floor! Needless to say, we took this as our cue to exit. We pantomimed our horror to the non-English speaking waitresses, who giggled and pointed, seeming not at all surprised about what was going on...\nRead more\nWritten October 7, 2018",
